> >> *(1) The program for a COVID 19 disaster payment, as specified in item 492 of the table in Part 4 of Schedule 1AB to the Financial Framework (Supplementary Powers) Regulations 1997, must comply with the following requirements:* >> >>> *(a) the payments must be available under the program in respect of a location in Australia that is subject to a State or Territory public health order restricting the movement of persons for a period of 7 days or more;* >>> >>> *(b) the payments must be available in respect of the period starting on the first day the restrictions are imposed by the order (and not limited only to the period starting after the end of the 7 day period);* >>> >>> *(c) the availability of the payments in respect of the location must not be made subject to the Commonwealth Chief Medical Officer first determining the location to be a COVID 19 hotspot;* >>> >>> *(d) the eligibility criteria must not include requirements that a person:* >>> >>>> *(i) has less than $10,000 of liquid assets; or* >>>> >>>> *(ii) does not receive a Commonwealth income support payment or payment of a similar nature.* >> >> *(2) Subsection (1) applies notwithstanding item 492 of the table in Part 4 of Schedule 1AB to the Financial Framework (Supplementary Powers) Regulations 1997 and prevails to the extent of any inconsistency with that item.* >> >> *(3) The program for a COV","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-7345","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2021-06-24/12"}
